            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "test/expected-schema-errors.txt",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you add  to the commit message why this is failing and why it can't just be fixed?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/expected-schema-errors.txt",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks like it's the following record which does not have the \"Name\" property.\n\n```\n            {\n                \"Address\": \"0x44\",\n                \"Bus\": 11,\n                \"Labels\": [\n                    \"in1\"\n                ],\n                \"Type\": \"ISL28022\",\n                \"in1_Max\": 1,\n                \"in1_Min\": -1,\n                \"in1_Name\": \"MEDUSA_ADC_48V_SENSE_VOLT_V\"\n            },\n```\n\nI did not want to fix it as part of this commit since this patch is about the schemas.\n\nIf i were to introduce a \"Name\" property there, that is also a review concern,\nand meta probably has their own naming schema for things like that. And i did not want to get blocked on waiting for someone from meta to look into it.\n\nSo i was hoping they will fix this on their own when they notice their config failing to validate.\n\n> Can you add to the commit message why this is failing\n\nDone \ud83d\udc4d\n\nLet me know if you have other thoughts. I can add some folks to this review who own / contribute to the meta configs, so they will be aware that their config is broken and then they can fix it in another patch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/expected-schema-errors.txt",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Opened https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/79287\nto fix the missing ```Name``` property.\n\nLet's not get blocked on it though. \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/expected-schema-errors.txt",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Rebased the patch since the failing config has been fixed.\n\nNow all configs are passing the validator as before \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
